  "body": "**Blocked by:** #101\n\n## Context\n\nHardcoded label comparisons cannot express stable processing behavior.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd `processingMethod` with values `pageContent` and `database`, plus nullable relation `targetDatabase`. Require a target database exactly for `database` and clear/reject it for `pageContent`. Archived types disappear from `GET /api/inbox-types` but remain valid references for existing items. Deleting a referenced type must route affected unlocked Inbox items through the same unknown-type processing path as a missing type; do not leave a dereferenced special case. Runtime target-project/page choice remains content-driven, not stored on the type.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Type validation, active picker behavior, archive, delete, and unknown-type semantics.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- LLM prompt engineering and target-selection implementation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Invalid method/target combinations fail validation.\n- Archived types are absent from new capture but old relations remain readable.\n- Deleted references deterministically enter clarification processing.\n- Type decisions use id and method, never localized label text.\n",
